			<item>
				<title>Mamba Hybrid Model State</title>
				<link>https://zhixuan-zxli.github.io/llm/mamba_hybrid/</link>
				<pubDate>Sat, 22 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://zhixuan-zxli.github.io/llm/mamba_hybrid/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;mambahybrid-align-mode-state-management-torch-reference&#34;&gt;MambaHybrid: Align-Mode State Management (torch reference)&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This document translates &lt;code&gt;MambaHybridModelState.preprocess_state&lt;/code&gt; and&#xA;&lt;code&gt;postprocess_state&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;vllm/v1/worker/gpu/model_states/mamba_hybrid.py&lt;/code&gt;) into&#xA;pure-torch reference implementations. The production versions launch fused&#xA;Triton kernels (&lt;code&gt;vllm/v1/worker/mamba_utils.py&lt;/code&gt;) that do everything GPU-side&#xA;with no CPU-GPU sync (async-scheduling safe); the torch versions below are&#xA;semantically equivalent but sync (&lt;code&gt;.item()&lt;/code&gt;), so they are for understanding /&#xA;debugging / CPU fallback, not performance.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;overview&#34;&gt;Overview&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Mamba/hybrid models store recurrent state (conv windows + SSM temporal state)&#xA;in KV-cache blocks: each &lt;code&gt;(layer, state-type)&lt;/code&gt; state tensor is block-major,&#xA;&lt;code&gt;[num_blocks, ...]&lt;/code&gt;, indexed through the request&amp;rsquo;s block table.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Model Runner V2</title>
				<link>https://zhixuan-zxli.github.io/llm/model_runner_v2_walkthrough/</link>
				<pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://zhixuan-zxli.github.io/llm/model_runner_v2_walkthrough/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;model-runner-v2-code-walkthrough&#34;&gt;Model Runner V2: Code Walkthrough&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This document explains the execution path of Model Runner V2 (MRV2), centered on&#xA;&lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/releases/v0.27.0/vllm/v1/worker/gpu/model_runner.py&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;vllm/v1/worker/gpu/model_runner.py&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&#xA;It is intended as a code-reading guide. The higher-level design rationale is in&#xA;&lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/releases/v0.27.0/vllm/docs/design/model_runner_v2.md&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;model_runner_v2.md&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;MRV2 is a per-worker orchestration layer. It does not implement transformer&#xA;layers. Instead, it connects scheduler state, GPU-resident request state,&#xA;attention/KV-cache metadata, CUDA graphs, the model, sampling, and output&#xA;processing.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;1-code-structure&#34;&gt;1. Code structure&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-mermaid&#34; data-lang=&#34;mermaid&#34;&gt;flowchart TD&#xA;    S[&amp;#34;SchedulerOutput&amp;#34;] --&amp;gt; R[&amp;#34;GPUModelRunner.execute_model&amp;#34;]&#xA;    R --&amp;gt; U[&amp;#34;Update request and KV state&amp;#34;]&#xA;    U --&amp;gt; I[&amp;#34;prepare_inputs&amp;#34;]&#xA;    I --&amp;gt; A[&amp;#34;prepare_attn&amp;#34;]&#xA;    A --&amp;gt; D[&amp;#34;dispatch_cg_and_sync_dp&amp;#34;]&#xA;    D --&amp;gt; M[&amp;#34;ModelState.prepare_inputs / prepare_attn&amp;#34;]&#xA;    M --&amp;gt; F[&amp;#34;Model forward: eager, PIECEWISE, or FULL CUDA graph&amp;#34;]&#xA;    F --&amp;gt; X[&amp;#34;ExecuteModelState&amp;#34;]&#xA;    X --&amp;gt; T[&amp;#34;sample_tokens&amp;#34;]&#xA;    T --&amp;gt; L[&amp;#34;Compute logits and sample&amp;#34;]&#xA;    L --&amp;gt; P[&amp;#34;postprocess_sampled&amp;#34;]&#xA;    P --&amp;gt; G[&amp;#34;Speculator proposal and KV connector&amp;#34;]&#xA;    G --&amp;gt; O[&amp;#34;AsyncOutput / ModelRunnerOutput&amp;#34;]&#xA;&#xA;    R -. &amp;#34;last PP rank&amp;#34; .-&amp;gt; T&#xA;    R -. &amp;#34;non-last PP rank&amp;#34; .-&amp;gt; PP[&amp;#34;IntermediateTensors&amp;#34;]&#xA;&#xA;    RS[&amp;#34;RequestState&amp;#34;] --&amp;gt; I&#xA;    IB[&amp;#34;InputBuffers / InputBatch&amp;#34;] --&amp;gt; I&#xA;    BT[&amp;#34;BlockTables / KV cache&amp;#34;] --&amp;gt; A&#xA;    CG[&amp;#34;ModelCudaGraphManager&amp;#34;] --&amp;gt; D&#xA;    MS[&amp;#34;DefaultModelState or model-specific state&amp;#34;] --&amp;gt; M&#xA;    K[&amp;#34;Triton input/update kernels&amp;#34;] --&amp;gt; I&#xA;    K --&amp;gt; P&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;The main state objects have deliberately different lifetimes:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Chunk KDA Kernels</title>
				<link>https://zhixuan-zxli.github.io/llm/kda_chunk_fwd_kernels/</link>
				<pubDate>Sun, 09 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://zhixuan-zxli.github.io/llm/kda_chunk_fwd_kernels/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;chunk_kda_fwd-kernel-walkthrough&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;chunk_kda_fwd&lt;/code&gt; Kernel Walkthrough&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;A kernel-by-kernel analysis of &lt;code&gt;chunk_kda_fwd&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;fla/ops/kda/chunk_fwd.py:20&lt;/code&gt;), focused on the KDA path and context parallelism (CP). For each Triton kernel: a reference torch implementation, input/output shapes, and the grid layout.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;notation-and-global-shapes&#34;&gt;Notation and global shapes&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;$q, k \in \mathbb{R}^{B \times T \times H \times K}$ — queries/keys, $H$ q/k heads, head dim $K$&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;$v \in \mathbb{R}^{B \times T \times H_V \times V}$ — values, $H_V = H \cdot G$ value heads (GQA group size $G$), value dim $V$&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;$g \in \mathbb{R}^{B \times T \times H_V \times K}$ — per-channel log-decay gate (per value head)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;$\beta \in \mathbb{R}^{B \times T \times H_V}$ — delta-rule write strength&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;$\text{BT} = \text{chunk\_size}$ (default 64), $\text{BC} = 16$ (sub-chunk), $\text{NC} = \text{BT}/\text{BC}$ (4 when BT=64)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;$\text{RCP\_LN2} = 1/\ln 2$ — scaling that turns $\exp(\cdot)$ into $\exp_2(\cdot)$ for kernel speed&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The KDA recurrence being chunked is (per value head, dropping batch):&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
